# `@: Model m (@ Model) (@ Model)`, two addresses: a reference declaration whose candidate is one value and one more
# is refused at the extra value, whether or not anything reads the name (DECLARATION-CANDIDATE-ROLE,
# steps/defects.md). It was taken for a machine local with the model; the translation passed.
Model:
    int: value 7
end: Model
fn: check () int
    @: Model m (@ Model) (@ Model)
    return: 7
end: check
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: check(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
